00:53:54,000 --> 00:54:00,000
The Whole Nine Yards is a 2000 American crime
comedy film directed by Jonathan Lynn.

12
00:58:48,000 --> 00:58:54,000
It was written by Mitchell Kapner and stars Bruce Willis, Matthew Perry,
Amanda Peet, Michael Clarke Duncan, and Natasha Henstridge.

13
01:03:42,000 --> 01:03:48,000
The story follows a mild-mannered dentist as he travels to Chicago to inform a mob boss about
the whereabouts of his new neighbor, a former hitman with a price on his head.

14
01:08:36,000 --> 01:08:42,000
The film was produced by Franchise Pictures, Rational Packaging and Lansdown Films
and was distributed by Morgan Creek Productions through Warner Bros.

15
01:13:30,000 --> 01:13:36,000
It was released on February 18, 2000.

16
01:18:24,000 --> 01:18:30,000
The film received mixed reviews from critics and grossed $106 million.

17
01:23:18,000 --> 01:23:24,000
A sequel, The Whole Ten Yards, was released in 2004.

18
01:28:12,000 --> 01:28:18,000
The film explores themes of chicago, illinois,
gangster, montreal, canada, mafia, dentist.

